            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary atherosclerosis and total serum cholesterol in men and women].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study shows that the extent of atherosclerotic changes in the coronary arteries, revealed during coronaroangiography, has a significant correlation with the serum level of total cholesterol (TC). In patients with normal (less than 5.2 mmol/ l) TC the number of involved arteries and the number of stenotic segments are significantly smaller than those in patients with a TC level higher than 6.5 mmol/l.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
